<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
            <span class="kicker">What you get</span>
            <h2>Stop building identity from scratch</h2>
            <p>Sign-in screens, password policies, two-factor authentication, external providers, user management and permission
                checks: all ready, all standards-based.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-3">
            <article class="card reveal"><div class="icon">@SiteArt.Icon("key")</div><h3>OpenID Connect provider</h3>
                <p>Standard OIDC / OAuth 2.0 for web, SPA, mobile and server apps. Authorization Code + PKCE, refresh tokens, token exchange and service accounts.</p></article>
            <article class="card reveal" style="--d:.06s"><div class="icon">@SiteArt.Icon("login")</div><h3>Flexible sign-in</h3>
                <p>Passwords, passwordless sign-in with e-mail or SMS codes, two-factor authentication over e-mail / SMS, password reset and account lockout.</p></article>
            <article class="card reveal" style="--d:.12s"><div class="icon">@SiteArt.Icon("globe")</div><h3>External identity providers</h3>
                <p>One-click sign-in with Google, Microsoft, Apple, LinkedIn, Facebook, GitHub, X, any OpenID Connect provider and SAML.</p></article>
            <article class="card reveal"><div class="icon">@SiteArt.Icon("users")</div><h3>User pools</h3>
                <p>A separate pool for each product or audience, each with its own registration, password, session and redirect policy, fully isolated.</p></article>
            <article class="card reveal" style="--d:.06s"><div class="icon">@SiteArt.Icon("graph")</div><h3>Relationship-based authorization</h3>
                <p>A versioned authorization schema on OpenFGA. Answer "can this user edit this document?" with a single API call.</p></article>
            <article class="card reveal" style="--d:.12s"><div class="icon">@SiteArt.Icon("panel")</div><h3>Admin console</h3>
                <p>A web console for tenants, pools, applications, roles, scopes and users, with CSV bulk import and e-mail invitations.</p></article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section alt">
    <div class="wrap why">
        <div class="reveal">
            <span class="kicker" style="color:var(--teal);font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.85rem">Why Booster Auth</span>
            <h2>You keep control, everyone keeps the standard</h2>
            <p class="muted" style="font-size:1.1rem">Cloud identity services get you started fast, but they tie your data, your costs and your roadmap to someone else.
                Booster Auth gives you the same capabilities on your own infrastructure.</p>
            <div class="stat-row">
                <div class="stat-box"><b>100%</b><span>of your data on your servers</span></div>
                <div class="stat-box"><b>9</b><span>external identity providers</span></div>
                <div class="stat-box"><b>~10 min</b><span>from download to first sign-in</span></div>
                <div class="stat-box"><b>0</b><span>calls to a license server</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why-list">
            <div class="why-item reveal"><span class="num">1</span><div><h3>Your data stays home</h3><p>Users, passwords and sessions live in your own database, which makes GDPR and internal security policies easier to meet.</p></div></div>
            <div class="why-item reveal" style="--d:.06s"><span class="num">2</span><div><h3>Offline license, uninterrupted sign-in</h3><p>The license is verified inside the product, with no internet or license server. Even if a paid license expires, end-user sign-ins keep working.</p></div></div>
            <div class="why-item reveal" style="--d:.12s"><span class="num">3</span><div><h3>Locked to standards, not to us</h3><p>Any OIDC / OAuth 2.0 library or framework works out of the box. You can move whenever you want.</p></div></div>
            <div class="why-item reveal" style="--d:.18s"><span class="num">4</span><div><h3>Predictable cost</h3><p>No monthly per-user fees: one annual license per installation. Every feature in every plan.</p></div></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head reveal">
            <span class="kicker">Easy to start</span>
            <h2>Live in four steps</h2>
            <p>Download, install, get your license. You can run the whole system even on your own laptop.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid-2" style="align-items:center">
            <div class="steps" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr">
                <div class="step reveal"><h3>Download</h3><p>Download and unzip the package.</p></div>
                <div class="step reveal" style="--d:.06s"><h3>Install</h3><p>The <code>kurulum</code> script prepares your .env file.</p></div>
                <div class="step reveal" style="--d:.12s"><h3>Start</h3><p><code>docker compose up -d</code> starts every service.</p></div>
                <div class="step reveal" style="--d:.18s"><h3>License</h3><p>"Get a license" in the console: a trial or a plan.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="terminal reveal" style="--d:.1s">
                <div class="terminal-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
<pre><span class="c"># 1. Unzip the package</span>
<span class="p">$</span> unzip booster-auth.zip &amp;&amp; cd booster-auth
<span class="c"># 2. Enter your addresses, secrets are generated</span>
<span class="p">$</span> ./kurulum.sh
<span class="ok">.env olusturuldu.</span>
<span class="c"># 3. Start the whole system</span>
<span class="p">$</span> docker compose up -d
<span class="ok">✔ Container booster-auth-booster-idp-1  Started</span>
<span class="c"># 4. Console: http://localhost:3000</span></pre>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

